==Cimbrian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|cim|gmh|der}}, from {{inh|cim|goh|der}}, {{m|goh|ther}}. Cognate with {{cog|de|der}}, {{cog|nl|die}}, {{cog|en|the}}, {{cog|sv|den}}. {{doublet|cim|dèar|pos1=demonstrative pronoun}}.

===Article===
{{head|cim|articles}}

# {{lb|cim|Luserna|7}} [[the]]; {{n-g|[[definite article]] for two declensions}}:
## {{n-g|nominative singular masculine}}
##: {{ux|inline=1|cim|'''Dar''' mann is stérchor dan 's baip.|'''The''' man is stronger than the woman.}}
##: {{ux|inline=1|cim|'''Dar''' tòibel hat borlóart in sbantz.|'''The''' devil lost his tail.}}
## {{n-g|dative singular feminine}}
##: {{ux|inline=1|cim|Bar soin vo '''dar''' Tezza.|We're from Tezza|lit=We're from '''the''' Tezza.}}

====Usage notes====
Note: The genitive case has been largely lost in Cimbrian, however '''dar''' can function in the genitive (for all numbers and genders) before possessive pronouns, e.g. {{m|cim||khua '''dar''' maindarn|cow '''of''' mine}}.

